packaging/deb/output/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
# ANCHORED to the repo root with a leading slash. Unanchored, each of these
# matches a directory of that name at ANY DEPTH — so a nested backend/core/lib/
# or agent/internal/build/ would be silently untracked, with no error, no warning
# and no diff. dokk had a live instance: scripts/lib/s3_retry.sh was untrackable
# and would never have been committed, while local tests stayed green because the
# file was on disk. The gap only appears in a fresh checkout.
#
# The class CI does not catch is an asset consumed by BUNDLING rather than by an
# import — nothing references it, so nothing fails, and it goes missing from the
# artifact. A missing code file fails loudly; a missing packaged asset does not.
#
# Checked before anchoring: vnbui has no nested directory by any of these names,
# so this is prophylactic rather than a repair. frontend/dist/ is unaffected — it
# is ignored by frontend/.gitignore, not by the root `dist/` rule.
/build/
/develop-eggs/
/dist/
/downloads/
/eggs/
/.eggs/
/lib/
/lib64/
/parts/
/sdist/
/var/
/wheels/
pip-wheel-metadata/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

